{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183375-tarot-cards-as-a-game-mechanic","id":1183375,"title":"Tarot Cards as a game mechanic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-07T14:07:11-08:00","id":1183375,"title":"Tarot Cards as a game mechanic?","content":"Hi, everyone! I'm fascinated by the symbolism in the major/minor arcana, and when I was first putting together a Mage: The Awakening game I wanted to come up with a way to incorporate them into the gameplay. I'm not very good at non-narrative stuff, and when I first tried to do this I hit some snags.<br /> <br /> My initial idea was that players could choose a card that reflected their character's archetype, essentially replacing the Virtue/Vice aspect. I later figured that instead, the card should have two effects, one for when it was upright and the other for when it was inverted. The player could gain some kind of benefit when it was upright, but in calling on that would then have to invert the card, which would remain that way and provide a negative effect until they fulfilled some kind of condition. I had concerns, though, about balancing these effects, and if I'm being 100% honest I just really didn't want to do twenty-two of these when probably only three or four would ever get picked.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever done something similar, or have ideas on what would be interesting to try?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23842-marigold","name":"Marigold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T14:12:25-08:00","id":1183381,"title":"","content":"I remember something in Keys to the Supernal Tarot. Have you read it? It has great ideas and story hooks to mine for, and doubles as an introduction to Tarot in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T14:23:22-08:00","id":1183384,"title":"","content":"I took a look just now! While it's got some interesting ideas, it didn't really have anything to help with what I'm specifically looking for. Thanks for the suggestion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23842-marigold","name":"Marigold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T14:25:57-08:00","id":1183387,"title":"","content":"Actually- you know what would go with this pretty well? Lenormand cards. It also simplifies things a bit and though it doesn't do the major arcana thing- it'd definitely be pretty interesting in play, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23845-victoria","name":"Victoria","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T14:44:56-08:00","id":1183391,"title":"","content":"My issue with the Lenormand cards is that they have no inverted meanings and are intended to be more practical instead of symbolic/spiritual, so they don't serve my purposes, but thank you for the suggestion! Maybe for another kind of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23842-marigold","name":"Marigold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T16:24:15-08:00","id":1183419,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of having Mage-specific Anchors and having them be Tarot-themed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The simplest idea that comes to mind is to have the normal card be the &quot;virtue&quot; (regain all willpower) and have the inverted version be the &quot;vice&quot; (one willpower).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:06:35-08:00","id":1183428,"title":"","content":"Doesn\u2019t specifically refer to the OP post, but I know that a friend of mine does drawings to seek inspiration for the storylines that he puts his players through when using Mage or other systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:07:02-08:00","id":1183429,"title":"","content":"Hmm... something like...<br /> <br /> Archetype: The Fool<br /> Straight: Once per chapter, regain all spent Willpower points by starting a new project, or taking initiative in the course of existing events. <br /> Reversed: Once per scene, regain one spent Willpower point by heading into an unfamiliar situation without bothering to assess it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:09:20-08:00","id":1183430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183375-tarot-cards-as-a-game-mechanic?p=1183428#post1183428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t specifically refer to the OP post, but I know that a friend of mine does drawings to seek inspiration for the storylines that he puts his players through when using Mage or other systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a game, but I used to do something like that when writing etudes and characters, inspired directly by the Minor Arcana\u2019s Story Hooks in Keys to the Supernal Tarot. Fun stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:11:10-08:00","id":1183431,"title":"","content":"He does use it for individual NPCs as well to establish what their goals or attitudes are, it\u2019s a handy shortcut for figuring out how to initially present them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:21:46-08:00","id":1183436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183375-tarot-cards-as-a-game-mechanic?p=1183431#post1183431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He does use it for individual NPCs as well to establish what their goals or attitudes are, it\u2019s a handy shortcut for figuring out how to initially present them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Archetypes and stereotypes are handy for presenting less important characters. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of character depth, another fun idea; blending cards and archetypes, such as...<br /> <br /> Concept: Young and Proud Prince<br /> Straight (The Fool): Once per chapter, regain all spent Willpower points by taking initiative of a course of events, or kicking a new chain of events into action. <br /> Reversed (The Chariot): Once per scene, regain one spent Willpower point by ignoring others\u2019 advices just to prove that you are right or capable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T01:46:32-08:00","id":1183513,"title":"","content":"Back in old WW forum there were rules for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/692883-tarot-for-willpower\">using Tarot as Willpower for characters</a> - I may dig later my hard drive and try to repost them in general CoD topic. Basic idea was that each player take the same number of Tarot cards as Willpower points. Suitable to action card used get character a 9-Again on roll, beside normal +3 to roll. I then added bonus association to Arcana used, based on Paths. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Suit - Path - Arcana:</b><ul><li><b>Cups </b>- Thyrsus - Life and Spirit</li> <li><b>Major Arcana</b> - Acanthus - Fate and Time</li> <li><b>Pentacles \\ Coins </b>- Moros - Death and Matter</li> <li><b>Swords </b>- Mastigos - Mind and Space</li> <li><b>Wands </b>- Obrimos - Force and Prime</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-08-2018, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T16:06:47-08:00","id":1183749,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Agenda Conditions from Demon? They have that system of being a persistent part of your character with one effect when passively on, and a different effect you can trigger to use. You could start with that, have a passive and active effect for each direction and then have each player pick one. They could then switch it when desired but have the effects balance out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T13:02:29-08:00","id":1184054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183375-tarot-cards-as-a-game-mechanic?p=1183749#post1183749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at the Agenda Conditions from Demon? They have that system of being a persistent part of your character with one effect when passively on, and a different effect you can trigger to use. You could start with that, have a passive and active effect for each direction and then have each player pick one. They could then switch it when desired but have the effects balance out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hadn't considered that! I'll check those out, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23842-marigold","name":"Marigold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T13:28:00-08:00","id":1184502,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a small bit on 1st-edition Awakening-oriented Tarot symbolism for the White Wolf forums ages back, then brought it over to an online MUX set in Austria that I frequented at the time. I could re-post it here if you like, but was still fairly narrative-based and was meant more for players who enjoyed the cards and wanted correspondences with Paths, Practices, and Orders. I'd probably alter a few things for 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T15:45:35-08:00","id":1185371,"title":"","content":"Fyi, CofD writer Wood Ingham made a game about the last days of Atlantis called Chariot. It uses a Tarot based system. No dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}